    <title>《裸体午餐》《CRASH》：生的欲望死的欲望</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/690426f465ab4ef684b881ba</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">690426f465ab4ef684b881ba</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 31 Oct 2025 03:10:42 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="0">00:00</a> 《裸体午餐》</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="47">00:47</a> 原著作者：威廉布洛斯</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="187">03:07</a> 原著的两个重点之一：写作过程+写作动因</span></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="241">04:01</a> 写作动因：误杀琼</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="285">04:45</a> 大卫柯南伯格电影中的运用</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="454">07:34</a> 大卫柯南伯格的改编框架与逻辑：与原著关系不大，与作者关系更大</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="553">09:13</a> 原著的两个重点之二：写作手法</span></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="626">10:26</a> 关于cut-up（切割/拼贴手法）</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="908">15:08</a> 《裸体午餐》（威廉布洛斯）与《繁华圣母》（让热内）对比</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1194">19:54</a> 布洛斯与金斯堡的关系</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1374">22:54</a> 大卫柯南伯格的双重借鉴：将布洛斯的作品与布洛斯本人做了拼贴</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1526">25:26</a> 关于《裸体午餐》选择打字机作为载体的原因</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1591">26:31</a> 《酷儿》原著</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1802">30:02</a> 延伸乱聊（可跳过）</span></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1802">30:02</a> 找到自己总是看不懂爱情题材的作品的原因了</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1915">31:55</a> 布洛斯声称的写作动因的可疑</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2065">34:25</a> 乱比喻（Alexander McQueen VS John Galliano)</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2148">35:48</a> 《酷儿》电影</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2320">38:40</a> 《裸体午餐》名字解读</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2452">40:52</a> 《裸体午餐》带给我的另一层感受：中性化器官</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2515">41:55</a> 《CRASH》</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2544">42:24</a> 原著作者：巴拉德</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2597">43:17</a> 大卫柯南伯格的改编特点</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2734">45:34</a> 原著与改编电影的不同侧重点</span></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2745">45:45</a> 原著侧重点：车这个载体</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2894">48:14</a> 原著的野心</span></li><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2949">49:09</a> 对于原著的一些疑问</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3244">54:04</a> 鲍德里亚对《CRASH》的解读一：用近似医学报告的形式去描写性爱——大卫柯南伯格的重点选取：撞击</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3323">55:23</a> 鲍德里亚对《CRASH》的解读二：技术超越了功能性属性，伤口成为了新的性器官。技术如何重新塑造或者解构身体。</span></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3521">58:41</a> 关于“器官中性化”的题外话（可跳过）</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3583">59:43</a> 死亡驱力——《超越快乐原则》弗洛伊德</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4015">66:55</a> 鲍德里亚对《CRASH》的解读三：超现实主义消解虚构与现实二者</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4166">69:26</a> 《CRASH》(《CRASH》OST）Howard Shore</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episodes/6877f5a1a12f9ff06a867619" data-url="https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episodes/6877f5a1a12f9ff06a867619"><span>上一期大卫柯南伯格《大都会》《未来罪行》</span></a></p>]]></description>
